  "_about": "Component spec for pos-card-alert (modules/common-styling/content/alert.liquid + style/pos-card.css). Restored 2026-09-01 after being found as an orphaned, never-wired-up COMP_CONFIGS entry: the usage content below was already drafted but never got a spec JSON, preview markup, or nav entry. Documents the alert-card family (info/warning/error/success), matching content/alert.liquid's real type values and icon choices exactly. Built as a fully self-contained new-DS component: style/pos-card.css defines .pos-card-alert and its 3 modifiers directly (padding/radius/background/border/icon color), using semantic tokens only (--pos-color-{warning,important,confirmation}-muted). The Liquid partial (content/alert.liquid) is markup-only and CSS-agnostic. Regenerate spec-alert-card.liquid via scripts/generate-component.js's regen helper (RULES.md §6.5) if this file changes. 2026-09-03: two bugs fixed — (1) the Info icon used --pos-color-content-text-supplementary (a text-role token) instead of the correct decorative-icon token --pos-color-content-icon; (2) the message text used --pos-color-highlight-text, a figma:null same-value alias with no independent Figma binding, causing confusion in the Tokens panel — switched to the real, Figma-bound --pos-color-content-text, which resolves to the exact same value in every theme (light/dark/hc), so this is a pure naming correctness fix with zero visual change. 2026-09-03: border switched from --pos-color-frame (a real visible grey border) to --pos-color-frame-transparent across all four intents — invisible in light/dark (background color alone signals the intent), visible in HC mode, matching the same token already used by Avatar/Chip/Code/Popover/Segmented control. 2026-09-03: icon size reduced from a hardcoded 1.5rem to --pos-size-icon-m (20px), and the icon-to-text gap increased from .5em to --pos-primitive-size-15 (12px) — both now documented in shared.layout (previously undocumented). 2026-09-04: matched the real Figma alert component — added an optional bold title (title prop, stacked above the body text), an optional icon toggle (icon prop, default true — existing callers unaffected), and an optional left-aligned actions row (buttons prop, raw HTML, real .pos-button instances — composedOf now lists \"button\"). The Error intent icon changed from 'delete' (an X-in-circle, mismatched with the real design) to the new 'errorBadge' icon (same scalloped seal outline as checkBadge, with an exclamation glyph — derived from checkBadge's outer path + warning's exclamation glyph, both already-licensed assets, not new artwork) to match Figma. Without a title, .pos-card-alert-body behaves exactly like the bare <span> it replaces — fully backward compatible for any existing caller passing only `content`. 2026-09-04: title styling corrected — moved out of shared.layout (was miscategorized) into a new shared.title group referenced under each variant's Text heading: font-family/size match .pos-heading-4 exactly, weight is bold (overriding heading-4's own normal default), color matches .pos-heading-4's prominent-text color. 2026-09-04: fixed 3 stale/wrong token entries left over from earlier same-day edits — the actions gap was documented as --pos-gap-button-button (regular) but the real CSS uses --pos-gap-button-button-small (buttons were switched to pos-button-small per the general small-button-gap rule); the body-to-actions margin was documented as --pos-gap-section-elements but the real CSS uses --pos-gap-card-elements. Also added requiresSelector to every icon- and actions-specific token so the Tokens panel correctly adds/removes them when the Options-panel Icon/Buttons switches are toggled in the docs preview (previously the full static token list showed regardless of toggle state). 2026-10-01: alert card gets Figma's Flat elevation (--pos-primitive-shadow-flat, no hover change; was Small shadow briefly). 2026-10-02: title→text gap 16px (--pos-gap-text-text) → 12px (--pos-primitive-size-15